Track 1: Sun Dogs Swallow the Lighthouse
- Story & Context: When a rogue Pallasite bolide crashed into the bluffs near the Point Reyes lighthouse in 1961, Tobias Finch scavenged warm chunks of celestial iron, hauling them back to his workshop in a burlap sack still smelling of scorched brine and nickel. Working by kerosene lamp, Finch beat the extraterrestrial metal into an experimental bell for his York tuba, fitting the valves with escapement cogs from an 1820 Breguet chronometer to eliminate valve stickiness. Testing the franken-horn at dawn on the seaside promenade, the dizzying, bright staccato notes caused three exhausted lighthouse keepers to burst into laughter and begin dancing in the surf as Finch yelled through the mouthpiece: "The sky broke open just to set our clocks!"
