Track 2: Sister Finch at the Green Flash
- Story & Context: Tobias’s sister, Clara Finch, ran a quiet coastal apothecary and resented the noisy street musicians until an unseasonable tide forced her to fill in on second tuba during an open-air jam on Hermosa Pier. Gripping the cold meteorite-iron horn, she felt the exposed clockwork mechanism chatter rhythmically against her fingertips, releasing a sweet scent of lavender oil and warm clockwork grease as the Pacific sun slipped below the horizon. As an emerald burst of refracted light illuminated the pier, Clara caught the beat, locked eyes with her brother, and sang into the condenser mic with sudden, grinning abandon: "My heart has escapement teeth and you can't rewind the day."
