Track 3: Paranthelion on the Master Tape
- Story & Context: Decades after the boardwalk sessions faded into folklore, sound preservationist Dale Vance discovered a misplaced half-inch master tape inside an old redwood butter crate in Capitola, coated in dried sea salt and sparkling meteorite dust. Playing the fragile reel through studio monitors, Vance was hit by a blinding 180-BPM sonic tempest where three tubas and a flugelhorn chased each other across an optical halo of mock suns, so joyfully overdriven that the brass valves had magnetically imprinted their ticking rhythm onto the tape oxide. The track peaks as the ocean breeze drowns out the crowd and Tobias's voice rings out like a town crier: "Catch the extra light before the mainspring snaps!"
